{"name":"Tasman","hex":"#bac0b3","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tasman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Dutch.","A male given name transferred from the surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tasman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dianella tasmanica","blocks":[{"text":"Dianella tasmanica, commonly known as the Tasman flax-lily or Tasmanian flax-lily, is a herbaceous strappy perennial herb of the family Asphodelaceae, subfamily Hemerocallidoideae, found in southeastern Australia including Tasmania. Its leaves are up to 80 centimetres in length, and the flower stem is up to 1.5 m tall. Blue flowers in spring and summer are followed by violet berries. It adapts readily to cultivation and is commonly seen in Australian gardens. Unlike other Dianella species, its fruits are toxic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg/330px-Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianella_tasmanica"},{"title":"Tasman (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Tasman is a rare family name in the diaspora of Dutch people. The distribution of people with the surname varies from about 6000 in Indonesia to small numbers in Australia and New Zealand, while by 2007 only seven people with the name lived in the Netherlands. The most notable bearer of this name was the Dutch explorer Abel Tasman."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tasman_(name)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg/500px-Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg/500px-Dianella_tasmanica57110.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADianella_tasmanica57110.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg/500px-Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg/1280px-Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg/500px-Dianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADianella_tasmanica_01_Pengo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG/120px-Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG/250px-Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG/120px-Dianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADianella_tasmanica_-_Berlin_Botanical_Garden_-_IMG_8746.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dianella_tasmanica_02_Pengo.jpg/120px-Dianella_tasmanica_02_Pengo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Dianella_tasmanica_02_Pengo.jpg/250px-Dianella_tasmanica_02_Pengo.jpg?utm